<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pope Innocent X</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1574">1574</a>–<a href="/years/1655">1655</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Giovanni Battista Pamphili</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Innocent X, born Giovanni Battista Pamphili, was pope from 1644 to 1655. He prosecuted the Barberini nephews of his predecessor, protested against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peace-of-westphalia">Peace of Westphalia</a> and condemned five propositions of Jansenism, and his portrait was painted by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diego-velazquez">Diego Velázquez</a>. In 1649 his troops captured and razed Castro, ending the Farnese duchy there.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pope-innocent-x.jpg" alt="Pope Innocent X" width="320" height="408" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Diego Velázquez · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Retrato_del_Papa_Inocencio_X._Roma,_by_Diego_Vel%C3%A1zquez.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
